                        <provenance>The scroll belonged to <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15594TMBeru">Takla Māryām Bǝrru</persName>. According to the account on the manuscripts’
                            provenance given by Tisserant, this manuscript is among those acquired
                            by <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4805Grebaut">Sylvain Grébaut</persName> in <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1216AddisA">ʾAddis ʾAbabā</placeName> in <date when="1925"/>
                            with funds of <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS14055SaintJ">Jean Saint</persName>. The
                            manuscripts originated from <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC0241IHA">Šawā</placeName> (ʾAddis ʾAbabā, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2297DabraL">Dabra Libānos</placeName>, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2246DabraB">Dabra
                            Bǝrhān</placeName>), <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3549Gojjam">Goǧǧām</placeName> (<placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2687DimaG">Dimā Giyorgis</placeName>, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC7140Martula">Marṭula Māryām</placeName>, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC6927DabraWarq">Dabra Warq</placeName>) and <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1713Bagemd">Bagemdǝr</placeName>
                            (<placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3577Gondar">Gondar</placeName>, <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1669Azazo">ʾAzazo Takla Hāymānot</placeName>) and a few from <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC6569Tegray">Tǝgrāy</placeName>. </provenance>
                    </history>
